From 5a943231a9149bd90c370643ec81237d78b1ba40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:07:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 25/48] Debug page: never render the best frame

The best frame is a camera image of a person. The debug page showed it as
a thumbnail on the result and LivenessPage outcome cards (hidden only in
placeholder mode), and a P5-5 screenshot of the page captured it once. It
is now never rendered there, for any engine or build: both cards show
text only, with "best frame: N bytes" (or "none").

LivenessPage never rendered it: LivenessOutcome only carries the bytes to
the caller, and its toString prints the length. No other screen renders it.

flutter analyze clean; test/liveness 56/56.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/ui/liveness/liveness_debug_page.dart | 62 +++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/ui/liveness/liveness_debug_page.dart b/lib/ui/liveness/liveness_debug_page.dart
index a72bd9b..f0fa7af 100644
--- a/lib/ui/liveness/liveness_debug_page.dart
+++ b/lib/ui/liveness/liveness_debug_page.dart
@@ -719,57 +719,43 @@ class _LivenessDebugPageState extends State<LivenessDebugPage> {
     );
   }
 
+  // The best frame is a camera image of a person: it is never rendered on this page (any engine, any build),
+  // only its size is shown.
+  static String _bestFrame(Uint8List? jpeg) =>
+      'best frame: ${jpeg == null ? 'none' : '${jpeg.length} bytes'}';
+
